## Layers & components

<!--
One row per file/component this feature owns or introduces. tasks.md's Phases are broken down
directly from this table — every task must trace back to a row here. Mark anything not yet built
as "not yet created" / "needs modification" (Prospective mode, or a pending part of Retroactive
mode) rather than omitting it.

Dependency rule: delivery → usecase → domain. repository → domain. domain imports nothing from
the outer layers. Never put HTTP DTOs into domain/ or usecase/.
-->

| Layer | File | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Domain / Entity | `services/appService/domain/{{feature}}.go` | Pure business fields only. No JSON tags, no HTTP shapes. |
| Domain / Errors | `services/appService/domain/errors.go` | Sentinel errors this feature adds (e.g. `ErrXxxNotFound`, `ErrXxxConflict`). Handler maps these to HTTP status. |
| Domain / Repository interface | `services/appService/domain/{{feature}}.go` | Repository interface implemented by `repository/`. Defined here, not in `repository/`. |
| Domain / Mock | `services/appService/domain/mock_{{feature}}_repository.go` | Hand-written mock for usecase tests. |
| Usecase | `services/appService/usecase/{{verb}}_{{feature}}_usecase.go` | Validation rules and business orchestration. Depends on the domain interface, never a concrete repository. |
| Repository | `services/appService/repository/postgres_{{feature}}_repository.go` | SQL, transactions, row↔entity mapping. Knows nothing about HTTP. |
| Delivery / Handler | `services/appService/delivery/http/{{feature}}_handler.go` | Parse request → call usecase → map domain error to status code. No business logic. |
| Delivery / DTO | `services/appService/delivery/http/{{feature}}_handler.go` | Request/response DTOs live here (or a sibling dto file), never in domain/usecase. |
| Wiring | `services/appService/cmd/main.go` | Route registration + constructor injection. Flag any `⚠️ DEV ONLY` block touched. |
| Migration | `migrations/000N_{{feature}}.sql` | Schema delta, if any. Delete this row if the feature adds no schema. |
| API spec | `docs/specs/api/openapi.yaml` | Endpoint contract, updated in the same change as the handler. |

## Request flow

<!--
If the feature's main flow triggers 2+ sequential external calls or side effects (rule 5/6), the
Mermaid sequence diagram in `flow.md` is the authoritative visual — replace this whole ASCII block
with a one-line pointer:

    > See `flow.md` for the Mermaid sequence diagram (a 1:1 mirror of the Step-by-step Flow below).

Keep this ASCII trace only for a single-query feature with no Step-by-step Flow and no `flow.md`.
The ASCII shows: HTTP entry point down to the database, naming the middleware that guards it and
where the usecase boundary sits. See the existing design.md files for the exact style to reuse.
-->

```
<METHOD> /v1/<path>
  └─ <RequireAuth middleware | public>
       └─ {{Feature}}Handler.<Action>   (delivery/http)
            ├─ decode + validate request DTO
            └─ {{Action}}{{Feature}}Usecase.Execute(ctx, ...)   (usecase)
                 ├─ domain validation → sentinel error on failure
                 └─ {{Feature}}Repository.<Method>(ctx, ...)     (repository)
                      └─ SQL against <table>
```

